tubs. The trunk surface between the pegs is smooth.", "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"defect": "Neither seed has a dead-frond skirt. No brown or grey collapsed fronds hang below the living crown.", "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}], "observations": ["render-1 (P-BASE, visibility hidden) is almost empty: sky and ground, with only a clipped corner showing two trunk or stub pieces at the lower right. It gives no usable evidence of the leaf-base pattern at close range.", "In both P-WHOLE renders the crown still reads at a glance as a radial palm-like rosette on a single stem. The lowest fronds on seed 1 droop below the crown base (render-0, render-3).", "At P-WHOLE, frond colour is hard to read: the thin leaflets show as dark charcoal strokes with a faint blue-grey cast against the sky. The close view in render-3 shows a grey-green tint.", "The trunk is a plausible mid reddish/grey-brown, similar to the distant trunk in reference-0. There are no lighter, weathered stub faces, which is an optional refinement at this finish floor.", "Both seeds show a slight basal widening at the ground (render-0, render-2).", "Compared with the anchor (anchor-0), the finish is flat-shaded but at a similar stylised level. Finish quality is not the limiting factor; morphology is.", "Reference-0 also has a curved, leaning trunk, so the inventory treats curvature as variation (trunk-lean-and-curve). The owner's rule of never wavy is authoritative for the owner-priority cells. The zig-zag and S-jog in the renders are much sharper than the smooth lean in reference-0."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown is sparse and see-through. The fronds are thin and mostly straight rays, with little progressive arching. The crown outline is a starburst, not a dense hemisphere.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length, leaflet size and frond count may be set too low. The owner names leaflet size and frond length as the first dials.", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"observation": "The leaflets are short, sparse needles. The fronds read as a thin comb and lack the plumose, V-sectioned mass of the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow"}, {"observation": "Both seeds have a wavy trunk. Seed 1 has an S-jog near the crown, and seed 42 has a sharp mid-trunk kink.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "The trunk organs are drawn as sparse, isolated pegs, not a covering diamond lattice of leaf-base wedges.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Leaf-base density or size may be far below what is needed to tessellate.", "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"observation": "No fibrous interstitial matting is drawn on the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"observation": "The stem is single and unbranched, with nearly constant diameter apart from a slight basal widening.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem"}, {"observation": "Nothing leafy or branch-like grows from the trunk. The pegs are leaf-base organs, and no epiphytes are drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "No dead-frond skirt is present below the crown on either seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}, {"observation": "Frond colour cannot be read reliably at P-WHOLE because the leaflets render as dark hairline strokes. The close view suggests grey-green.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "The P-BASE render is clipped and shows almost no geometry, so the close-range leaf-base cell cannot be assessed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"observation": "The trunk hue is within the reference range. Weathered, paler stub faces are absent, which is optional at the catalogue floor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering"}, {"observation": "Both seeds show a slight basal flare at ground contact.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "basal-flare"}, {"observation": "Fruit clusters are absent. This is a known gap (fn-111) and was not assessed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent"}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The crown is a sparse, thin, straight-rayed starburst of about 20–25 fronds. The references show a dense crown of long arching fronds with a hemispherical outline."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "st